WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:00.690
Hey guys,

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:02.980
welcome back to our
Business English channel.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.140
Today, I want to start
off with a question.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:10.500
Have you ever felt so busy that you
needed an extra pair of hands?

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.820
Have you ever felt the need
to clone yourself?

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:17.980
Well, maybe you need
to delegate more. In this series,

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.340
let's look at some top tips
to improve your delegation skills.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.140
First, start small.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:25.000
Hand over tasks that don't need to be

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:29.700
overseen and tasks that are not paramount
to the completion of your project.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:34.004
Can you make sure a copy of these gets sent
to all the clients by the end of the week?

00:00:34.004 --> 00:00:35.004
Thanks.

00:00:35.004 --> 00:00:38.420
Could you just draw up those proposals,

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:42.740
print them out, edit and double check
them, and then just get them ready

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.460
and have them sent out to all
the clients by the end of next week?

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:46.960
Thanks.

00:00:47.109 --> 00:00:49.460
This allows you the chance to get used to

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:53.420
handing over these responsibilities
and at the same time,

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:58.180
allows your team members a chance
to get used to taking on those tasks.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:02.940
Next, we need to play
to our team's strengths.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.960
Hey Cara, can you work on our
logo design, please?

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.100
Yeah, that's fine.
No problem.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:13.720
Hey, Cara, can you work
on our logo design, please?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.770
Seriously?

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.980
This will not only ensure that your team

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.620
members stay happy and motivated,
but handing over tasks to those who have

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:28.120
the necessary skills will also give you
peace of mind that these tasks can be

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:32.210
achieved within your time frame
and to a high enough standard.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.780
Let's stop right there, guys.

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.820
We're breaking down the language.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.460
Today we're looking at idioms.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:46.660
An idiom is when the figurative meaning
of what you are trying to say is different

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:50.020
to the literal meaning
of the phrase that you use.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.850
For example, I have a lot on my plate.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:58.460
I am not talking about a plate
that has a lot of food on it.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:03.140
I just mean recently,
I have had a lot of things to do.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.930
I have been very, very busy.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.170
I have had a lot on my plate.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:10.380
Great, let's jump straight back.

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:14.000
We've broken down the language.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.340
The more you delegate, remember,

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:22.100
at the end, you will end up
with a more well-rounded team.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.060
I want to leave you with another idiom today.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:27.450
Many hands make light work.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.060
Use your team members.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.940
Delegate those tasks.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:33.940
It will help you relieve stress and will

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:39.517
free up some time so that you can help
better manage your team's specific needs.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.700
I hope you enjoyed our video today, guys.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:57.060
Please stay tuned to follow
on for the next series.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:58.340
If you haven't already,

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:02.140
you can click on the link below
and subscribe to the channel

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:06.460
and feel free to take a look at the rest
of the video series on things like

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.900
conflict management by clicking
on the link that you see here.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.093
Thanks for watching.
I will see you next time.

